@host = http://localhost:4005
@base = {{host}}/odata/v4/booking
@floor = 40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001
@room = 50000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001
@user = 60000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001

### Health
GET {{host}}/health

### Login first; HTTP clients must retain the response cookie
POST {{host}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"userID":"{{user}}"}

### Session
GET {{host}}/auth/session

### Domain and company
GET {{base}}/CompanyDomains?$filter=domain eq 'example.com'&$expand=company

### Geographic hierarchy
GET {{base}}/Sites?$expand=buildings($expand=floors)&$orderby=city

### Resource location
GET {{base}}/Resources?$expand=floor($expand=building($expand=site))

### Read-only views
GET {{base}}/Rooms

### Workplaces
GET {{base}}/Workplaces

### Create room (ADMIN)
POST {{base}}/Resources
Content-Type: application/json

{"floor_ID":"{{floor}}","type":"ROOM","code":"H-A-1-WORKSHOP","name":"Workshop","capacity":12,"roomType":"MEETING"}

### Create workplace (ADMIN)
POST {{base}}/Resources
Content-Type: application/json

{"floor_ID":"{{floor}}","type":"WORKPLACE","code":"H-A-1-DESK-NEW","name":"Window desk","workplaceType":"HOT_DESK","monitorCount":2}

### Create own booking; repeating returns 409
# @name createdBooking
POST {{base}}/Bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{"resource_ID":"{{room}}","title":"Project planning","startAt":"2026-09-15T09:00:00+02:00","endAt":"2026-09-15T10:00:00+02:00","attendeeCount":4}

### Read bookings
GET {{base}}/Bookings?$expand=resource,user&$orderby=startAt&$count=true

### Cancel (VS Code REST Client response variable)
PATCH {{base}}/Bookings({{createdBooking.response.body.$.ID}})
Content-Type: application/json

{"status":"CANCELLED"}

### Reference hours
GET {{base}}/OpeningHours?$expand=site&$orderby=dayOfWeek

### Own weekly plan
POST {{base}}/WorkDays
Content-Type: application/json

{"date":"2026-09-15","mode":"HOME","startTime":"08:00:00","endTime":"17:00:00"}

### REST alias with the same JSON contract
GET {{host}}/api/v1/resources/{{room}}

### Atomic batch: the second booking conflicts, so both are rolled back
POST {{base}}/$batch
Content-Type: application/json

{"requests":[{"id":"a","method":"POST","url":"Bookings","atomicityGroup":"group1","body":{"resource_ID":"{{room}}","title":"A","startAt":"2026-10-01T09:00:00Z","endAt":"2026-10-01T10:00:00Z"}},{"id":"b","method":"POST","url":"Bookings","atomicityGroup":"group1","body":{"resource_ID":"{{room}}","title":"B","startAt":"2026-10-01T09:30:00Z","endAt":"2026-10-01T10:30:00Z"}}]}

### Logout
POST {{host}}/auth/logout
Content-Type: application/json

{}
